WEBVTT

00:04.850 --> 00:13.110
<b>A Playthrough of a Certain DUDE's
VRMMO LIFE</b>

01:29.980 --> 01:32.400
<b>Second Round Player
Registrations Now Open</b>

01:32.390 --> 01:34.400
<i>They're allowing about as many new players</i>

01:34.400 --> 01:36.230
<i>as there are existing players, huh?</i>

01:36.230 --> 01:38.830
<i>I guess that means the new 
servers have been installed.</i>

01:39.290 --> 01:43.020
<i>I heard that the shortage of 
VR headsets got resolved, too.</i>

01:43.020 --> 01:45.280
<i>Which means registrations 
won't be open for long.</i>

01:49.470 --> 01:50.650
Hey, Earth.

01:51.610 --> 01:52.660
Hey.

01:52.660 --> 01:56.060
They added a new status effect 
in yesterday's patch.

01:56.060 --> 01:57.200
How are you gonna handle it?

01:57.510 --> 01:59.440
Break Arms, huh?

01:59.440 --> 02:02.560
If you get hit with it, you can't 
hold a weapon for a while.

02:02.870 --> 02:06.060
We'll have to watch out for 
paralysis and petrification.

02:06.310 --> 02:11.890
It'll trigger if you take more than 25% of 
your total HP in damage to your arms, too.

02:11.890 --> 02:16.070
Well, at least other players 
can't steal your dropped weapon.

02:17.240 --> 02:21.640
I played another game where somebody swiped 
a rare weapon from me after I died.

02:21.860 --> 02:23.230
Really?

02:25.200 --> 02:29.670
<b>New Update Announcement
A new dungeon is coming!!</b>

02:26.060 --> 02:29.990
<i>It's time to announce our new update!
 A new dungeon is coming!</i>

02:29.670 --> 02:32.380
<b>Its name is
"A Challenge From the Departed"
!!!</b>

02:29.990 --> 02:32.380
<i>Its name is "A Challenge From the Departed!"</i>

02:32.680 --> 02:35.570
<i>The dungeon is entirely randomly generated.</i>

02:35.570 --> 02:38.260
<i>Each time you enter, it will be 
a completely new experience!</i>

02:38.260 --> 02:41.580
<i>And there are all kinds of traps 
awaiting unlucky players,</i>

02:41.580 --> 02:44.540
<i>so if you can't think quick, you'll be 
joining the dead in the dungeon!</i>

02:46.200 --> 02:49.520
<i>How far can </i>you<i> get before the 
one-hour time limit runs out?</i>

02:49.520 --> 02:52.010
<i>Your first goal will be the tenth floor!</i>

02:52.010 --> 02:55.350
<i>It's up to you whether you accept 
this challenge from the departed!</i>

02:55.350 --> 02:58.740
<i>Look forward to our next update!</i>

02:58.740 --> 03:01.240
A totally randomly generated dungeon...

03:01.240 --> 03:03.470
That sounds like a ton of fun!

03:03.470 --> 03:06.700
<i>Now, we'll do an advance 
showing of our trailer</i>

03:06.700 --> 03:08.920
<i>for the second round of 
player registrations!</i>

03:15.250 --> 03:16.420
That's me!

03:21.520 --> 03:23.130
Don't show that!

03:23.370 --> 03:26.640
Aw, you look so cool, though!

03:26.640 --> 03:29.060
If new players think bows are 
a lot stronger than they are,

03:29.060 --> 03:31.060
they're going to regret it later...

03:32.840 --> 03:35.000
<i>If I'm going to get ready 
for the new dungeon,</i>

03:35.510 --> 03:38.030
<i>then I'll need a shield!</i>

03:38.440 --> 03:42.330
<i>I don't think I can get any further in the 
game with dodging as my only defense,</i>

03:42.840 --> 03:46.170
<i>especially in a cramped dungeon 
without room to move around.</i>

03:54.680 --> 03:57.280
<i>I specialized my 
Shield Skill in "small shields,"</i>

03:57.280 --> 03:59.100
<i>which makes it easier to use my bow.</i>

03:59.820 --> 04:02.960
<i>Thanks to that, I can gather 
materials at the same time.</i>

04:03.280 --> 04:06.130
<i>Next, it's time to make 
new equipment, but...</i>

04:08.790 --> 04:10.980
What are you making this time?

04:10.980 --> 04:13.860
I'm making a new compound bow 
with these plans I brought in

04:13.860 --> 04:15.590
from the real world.

04:16.230 --> 04:23.780
<b>Otherworld Bow
 A bow created using methods not from our world.
The principles behind it are unknown, but it's
extremely powerful and stable.
However, it requires special arrows to use.
 Effect: Atk+38 Score: 3</b>

04:17.400 --> 04:21.040
Its attack is that high 
even with a score of 3?

04:21.040 --> 04:23.780
Any archer would love this!

04:23.780 --> 04:27.660
I can't recommend it to them, 
given how much the arrows cost.

04:27.660 --> 04:30.890
And I just made it to learn more 
about how these things work.

04:30.890 --> 04:32.190
I'm not going to use it.

04:32.190 --> 04:35.860
You mean you're trying to 
make something even better?

04:35.860 --> 04:39.830
Yeah, but it doesn't exist in the real world,

04:39.830 --> 04:42.120
so I'll have to draw up the plans myself.

04:46.790 --> 04:50.050
It's finally done! That took forever!

04:50.890 --> 04:53.680
<b>Secret Light Metal Shield
 A small shield made from light metal. Usable as a shield, but also has a secret functionality.
 Effect: Def+25
 Special Effects: Transformation Ability, Right Arm Only
 Score: 6</b>

04:53.900 --> 04:57.090
<i>I used material from the 
rock ants' exoskeletons</i>

04:57.090 --> 04:59.110
<i>on the sides of the shield to strengthen it,</i>

04:59.110 --> 05:03.610
<i>but mostly to protect the compound bow 
parts that I've placed inside the back.</i>

05:05.200 --> 05:07.530
<b>Secret Another Bow
 The shield with its secret mechanism deployed.
For a hunting bow, it's small, but it's extremely lethal and accurate.
 However, it requires special arrows to use.
 Effect: Atk+60 Def+5
 Special Effects: Transformation Ability, Right Arm Only, Accuracy Bonus (Weak)
 Score: 6</b>

05:07.530 --> 05:13.400
<i>Maybe the Accuracy Bonus (Weak) came from 
the little scope sight I put on it?</i>

05:13.870 --> 05:18.820
<i>If I let go of the grip, it goes 
back to being a normal shield.</i>

05:19.420 --> 05:22.120
<i>The reason I raised my shield 
skill on my right hand,</i>

05:22.120 --> 05:24.440
<i>and made that compound bow for practice,</i>

05:24.860 --> 05:28.090
<i>and went through all that trouble trying 
to figure out how to draw plans,</i>

05:28.090 --> 05:29.840
<i>was all for this.</i>

05:30.200 --> 05:33.360
<i>It works in a semi-weird way, 
and the handle's upside-down,</i>

05:33.360 --> 05:36.050
<i>but it's a weapon intended 
just for me, so that's fine!</i>

05:39.930 --> 05:43.660
Okay, now even if I get hit with Break Arms,

05:43.660 --> 05:47.520
I won't immediately lose my 
ability to attack at long range!

05:47.860 --> 05:52.580
<i>It took five whole days to finish it, 
but it's good to be ready.</i>

05:53.660 --> 05:55.910
<b>Installing Update</b>

05:59.670 --> 06:01.880
<b>Complete</b>

06:02.380 --> 06:06.380
<b>Episode 6</b>

06:02.380 --> 06:06.380
<b>Earth Gets Excited Over a New Dungeon</b>

06:07.280 --> 06:08.840
Look at all the players!

06:09.240 --> 06:12.770
I guess that's what happens the 
first day after a big update.

06:12.770 --> 06:15.760
Now, time to check out that new dungeon!

06:16.160 --> 06:18.050
We're having a big sale!

06:18.050 --> 06:19.900
Don't go in there without potions!

06:19.900 --> 06:21.850
Who wants potions?

06:21.850 --> 06:25.020
Cheap, powerful potions!

06:23.610 --> 06:25.840
Buy now or cry later!

06:25.840 --> 06:28.450
Who wants to try my new potions?

06:26.680 --> 06:29.210
<i>The merchant players are all fired up, too.</i>

06:29.210 --> 06:31.990
<i>This is where they make their money.</i>

06:31.990 --> 06:32.720
You there!

06:32.720 --> 06:34.050
Listen to me!

06:39.390 --> 06:42.660
Um... what is it?

06:42.660 --> 06:44.310
I am Red!

06:45.340 --> 06:46.090
<b>Red</b>

06:46.080 --> 06:47.570
I'm Blue!

06:48.760 --> 06:49.510
<b>Blue</b>

06:49.500 --> 06:51.270
Mah name is Yellow!

06:52.180 --> 06:52.930
<b>Yellow</b>

06:52.940 --> 06:54.650
I'm Pink!

06:55.640 --> 06:56.350
<b>Pink</b>

06:56.350 --> 06:58.030
And I am none other than Green!

06:59.060 --> 06:59.770
<b>Green</b>

07:00.800 --> 07:02.340
Together, we are...

07:02.340 --> 07:06.220
Stop, stop! You can't say another word!

07:06.550 --> 07:08.090
But we're just getting to the good part!

07:08.090 --> 07:09.890
Absolutely not!

07:09.900 --> 07:14.910
<b>Gang of Six Rangers
One More Rangers</b>

07:14.910 --> 07:19.910
<b>Gang of Six Rangers
One More Rangers</b>

07:19.900 --> 07:21.570
I see!

07:21.570 --> 07:24.090
A party that's modeling themselves 
after Sentai rangers?

07:24.090 --> 07:26.510
Where's Black, then?

07:26.510 --> 07:29.490
He said he had a stomachache today.

07:29.490 --> 07:31.920
Well, don't worry about that, okay?

07:32.290 --> 07:34.960
<i>You guys don't really sound like rangers...</i>

07:34.960 --> 07:37.270
<i>But I guess I'm supposed 
to ignore that, right?</i>

07:37.530 --> 07:40.590
Anyway, that means we 
don't have enough people.

07:40.590 --> 07:44.520
We were looking for another 
member when we found you!

07:44.520 --> 07:46.440
And so, of course, we had to approach you!

07:46.770 --> 07:49.510
<i>I don't think I can get too 
far in there on my own,</i>

07:49.510 --> 07:51.110
<i>so maybe I'll go along with them.</i>

07:51.400 --> 07:54.530
You're inviting me to a 
pick-up group, right?

07:56.290 --> 07:58.320
You're not wrong.

07:59.610 --> 08:01.500
You're really into the role-play thing, huh?

08:01.500 --> 08:02.940
Then it's settled!

08:02.940 --> 08:05.030
We assault the enemy hideout, everyone!

08:05.030 --> 08:06.430
Right!

08:06.430 --> 08:09.470
It's not a hideout, though! It's a dungeon!

08:09.470 --> 08:11.290
Well, whatever.

08:18.060 --> 08:20.080
All right! Let's go—

08:20.080 --> 08:21.110
Wait!

08:23.730 --> 08:26.360
<b>Threat Detection</b>

08:26.570 --> 08:29.770
Looks like we hit a nasty map.

08:29.770 --> 08:32.420
There are fifteen traps in this room.

08:33.530 --> 08:36.290
And four of them are instant death traps.

08:36.290 --> 08:38.940
It's pretty typical for 
heroes to fall for traps,

08:38.940 --> 08:40.800
but I don't want us getting wiped out.

08:42.010 --> 08:45.030
True, that would be a problem.

08:45.390 --> 08:46.680
I'll take the lead.

08:46.680 --> 08:48.660
Follow my path exactly.

08:48.660 --> 08:49.730
Right.

08:56.340 --> 08:58.610
Red made the right call.

08:58.610 --> 09:03.320
I was concerned when he wanted to 
add another member, but...

09:03.320 --> 09:05.000
<i>I bet.</i>

09:05.000 --> 09:07.630
<i>You never know what'll happen when
 you add a new member for one session.</i>

09:07.630 --> 09:09.690
<i>I'm surprised they decided to do it at all.</i>

09:09.690 --> 09:14.030
No, we were lucky to meet the guy 
who married the Fairy Queen.

09:14.030 --> 09:15.750
There's no way he could be weak.

09:16.490 --> 09:19.840
Um, are you talking about me?

09:19.840 --> 09:21.530
Who else could I be talking about?

09:21.530 --> 09:23.860
I want to cry...

09:28.210 --> 09:30.120
We're finally through.

09:30.120 --> 09:32.680
We'll take the lead from now on.

09:32.680 --> 09:33.960
Sure.

09:33.960 --> 09:36.100
Come on! Swiftly!

09:36.100 --> 09:36.820
Swiftly!

09:36.820 --> 09:37.610
Swiftly!

09:46.480 --> 09:48.200
The enemy is here!

09:48.200 --> 09:51.060
We five warriors shall defeat our foes!

09:51.060 --> 09:52.010
Right!

09:53.470 --> 09:55.120
Too easy.

09:55.120 --> 09:57.060
Piece of cake!

09:58.250 --> 09:59.920
Behold my techniques!

10:04.310 --> 10:06.000
The power of justice prevails!

10:06.000 --> 10:09.950
Oh, I guess you call yourself 
heroes for a reason!

10:09.950 --> 10:13.750
I guess I can focus on finding traps, then!

10:16.160 --> 10:18.390
The stairs to the second floor!

10:18.390 --> 10:20.400
How long did it take us to get here?

10:20.400 --> 10:21.840
Eighteen minutes.

10:21.840 --> 10:25.550
We're taking too much time for 
a one-hour dungeon.

10:26.100 --> 10:30.460
Sorry. I wish I could 
disarm the traps faster,

10:30.460 --> 10:32.120
but it's dangerous to rush this stuff.

10:32.390 --> 10:35.490
None of us are so foolish as to 
complain about such a thing!

10:35.490 --> 10:36.780
Be at ease!

10:36.780 --> 10:38.690
We're just glad to have you.

10:38.960 --> 10:42.880
I think we've just got 
to be careful as we go.

10:43.240 --> 10:44.860
Okay, let's go down a floor!

10:47.750 --> 10:52.580
It took us eighteen minutes to find the staircase 
from the first floor to the second, but...

10:52.580 --> 10:55.330
We'll make it to the 
third floor really fast.

10:55.600 --> 10:59.640
Sometimes a randomly generated dungeon 
is on your side, and sometimes it's not.

10:59.640 --> 11:02.260
Let's hurry on ahead!

11:02.260 --> 11:03.610
Swiftly!

11:04.860 --> 11:05.880
Hwaah!

11:08.480 --> 11:10.770
Wights and skeleton soldiers!

11:10.770 --> 11:12.190
Leave it to me!

11:12.190 --> 11:14.240
All right... Here I go!

11:14.640 --> 11:17.230
Glorious Lovely Flash!

11:26.560 --> 11:28.090
Did we get them?

11:30.490 --> 11:31.560
Oh, my!

11:31.560 --> 11:34.360
The skeleton soldiers can 
dispel the spell, huh?

11:34.360 --> 11:37.450
They're different from the skeletons 
we saw on the first floor!

11:38.130 --> 11:39.640
More wights!

11:39.640 --> 11:40.860
Don't worry!

11:43.390 --> 11:45.830
We'll destroy them!

11:49.510 --> 11:51.720
My attacks aren't working!

11:57.040 --> 11:59.110
Wights can't take physical damage!

11:59.110 --> 12:02.440
Leave this to me and Pink, 
and Blue's water magic!

12:02.820 --> 12:03.920
Thanks!

12:04.200 --> 12:07.150
<i>This Aeolian Dust Arrow 
has wind magic on it,</i>

12:07.150 --> 12:09.040
<i>so it'll work on the wights!</i>

12:16.190 --> 12:20.020
So we've finally found the way 
down to the fourth floor?

12:20.020 --> 12:23.250
We lost a lot of time dealing 
with those tricky monsters.

12:23.980 --> 12:26.370
It's been forty minutes already.

12:26.370 --> 12:29.170
There's no way we'll make it 
to the tenth floor in time.

12:29.170 --> 12:32.150
Why don't we aim for the 
fifth floor instead?

12:32.150 --> 12:33.560
No objection here!

12:37.220 --> 12:40.730
<i>What is this feeling, like the 
grim reaper's caressing my face?</i>

12:41.530 --> 12:43.520
Something's not right about this floor.

12:43.520 --> 12:44.400
Right!

12:44.790 --> 12:46.590
Somebody help me!

12:50.090 --> 12:51.470
Another party?

12:51.470 --> 12:52.890
What happened?

12:52.890 --> 12:54.290
I'm coming!

12:54.290 --> 12:55.240
Wait!

13:04.880 --> 13:06.610
<i>That trap locked us in here!</i>

13:06.610 --> 13:09.850
<i>It's the type that won't let us leave 
until we complete this room's quest!</i>

13:15.850 --> 13:17.530
Look at them all.

13:17.940 --> 13:19.850
There's no time to think about this.

13:19.850 --> 13:20.560
Let's go, everyone!

13:20.870 --> 13:22.050
Understood!

13:22.050 --> 13:23.640
Time to kick butt!

13:24.930 --> 13:26.040
<i>Are there traps...?</i>

13:28.730 --> 13:29.960
<i>No!</i>

13:29.960 --> 13:32.440
I can fight with my full strength!

13:32.820 --> 13:34.520
Gatling Arrow!

13:34.520 --> 13:35.850
Aeolian Dust Arrow!

13:45.820 --> 13:47.860
Thanks, you saved us.

13:48.560 --> 13:50.130
Let's join the fight, too!

13:50.130 --> 13:51.710
Okay! Finish them!

13:53.230 --> 13:55.110
Storm...

13:56.940 --> 13:58.660
Hurricane!

14:02.600 --> 14:04.290
<i>That's one heck of a flashy attack...</i>

14:04.290 --> 14:06.460
<i>It does look strong, though!</i>

14:13.260 --> 14:14.820
You're the leader, huh?

14:14.820 --> 14:17.250
Thanks for saving us from being wiped out!

14:17.250 --> 14:19.210
I just did what anyone would do!

14:21.830 --> 14:23.620
Look, a huge treasure chest.

14:24.510 --> 14:26.810
I can't wait to see what's inside!

14:28.300 --> 14:30.300
<b>Threat Detection</b>

14:30.310 --> 14:32.730
No! Don't touch that chest!

14:33.480 --> 14:37.510
What, you think we owe you 
this because you saved us?

14:37.830 --> 14:40.050
No, it's a trap!

14:40.470 --> 14:42.710
Don't underestimate me.

14:42.710 --> 14:45.080
I've got thief skills, too.

14:45.080 --> 14:46.480
I can tell if there's a trap.

14:47.680 --> 14:48.940
Fine.

14:48.940 --> 14:51.220
We won't touch the chest.

14:52.590 --> 14:53.520
Earth!

14:53.820 --> 14:58.490
If you insist on opening it, 
wait until we're all out of the room!

14:58.870 --> 15:01.790
But then we won't get any reward...

15:03.050 --> 15:05.590
We should do what Earth says.

15:05.590 --> 15:06.680
Red.

15:07.860 --> 15:08.600
Right.

15:08.920 --> 15:11.010
Let's leave immediately.

15:11.940 --> 15:14.930
Earth, if you abandoned 
that treasure chest,

15:14.930 --> 15:16.730
there must be something 
really bad inside, right?

15:16.730 --> 15:17.950
Yeah.

15:17.950 --> 15:21.400
This room had a double trap.

15:21.400 --> 15:24.170
The first trapped you inside 
with a bunch of monsters.

15:24.170 --> 15:25.360
And the other...

15:30.420 --> 15:32.460
Kills you with your own greed.

15:34.390 --> 15:35.770
We're out of time.

15:37.730 --> 15:40.870
Earth, I don't want to offend you,

15:40.870 --> 15:42.470
but can I ask you a question?

15:43.850 --> 15:46.910
That adventurer said he had thief skills,

15:44.880 --> 15:46.460
<b>Threat Detection</b>

15:46.910 --> 15:48.790
but he didn't see the trap.

15:49.690 --> 15:52.470
I know it's considered impolite 
to ask about others' skills,

15:52.470 --> 15:55.130
but is your level above 20?

15:55.130 --> 15:59.570
I can't give you the exact number, 
but I'll admit it's over 20.

16:00.080 --> 16:02.320
<i>It's actually above 30.</i>

16:02.320 --> 16:05.720
<i>If it was 20, I wouldn't have 
been able to see that last trap.</i>

16:05.720 --> 16:08.740
<i>But I shouldn't tell that 
to somebody I've just met.</i>

16:09.020 --> 16:11.750
Let's split up our winnings 
and call it a day.

16:11.750 --> 16:13.650
We didn't get much, though.

16:13.650 --> 16:18.080
My thief skills went way up, 
so I'm pretty happy.

16:18.490 --> 16:20.860
If you're satisfied, then so are we!

16:21.230 --> 16:23.040
I'm not!

16:23.040 --> 16:25.340
I wanted to explore the second floor more!

16:25.340 --> 16:27.730
There might've been good items!

16:27.730 --> 16:30.150
But there's that time limit!

16:30.150 --> 16:34.090
Clearing an entire floor before moving on 
to the next is one way to enjoy a dungeon!

16:34.090 --> 16:36.050
I enjoy mapping!

16:36.050 --> 16:37.760
I get that!

16:37.760 --> 16:40.460
You feel so satisfied 
when you complete a map!

16:40.460 --> 16:43.980
Behold! This is my complete 
map of the first floor!

16:43.980 --> 16:47.110
I can never figure out what 
your maps are trying to say.

16:47.110 --> 16:48.800
Is this map really right?

16:48.800 --> 16:51.780
Green has a terrible 
sense of direction, too.

16:51.780 --> 16:56.510
These floors are randomly generated anyway, 
so that map'll be useless next time we come.

16:58.410 --> 16:59.690
Good point.

17:00.020 --> 17:02.510
Earth, thank you so much for coming today!

17:02.510 --> 17:04.720
We'd love to introduce you to Black!

17:04.720 --> 17:07.070
Let me send a friend request!

17:08.260 --> 17:09.590
Sure.

17:09.590 --> 17:12.560
I was lucky I got to do a run with you guys!

17:14.740 --> 17:17.750
If I want to get to the 
tenth floor within an hour,

17:17.750 --> 17:20.630
I need to be able to disarm traps faster.

17:20.630 --> 17:26.280
That's why I decided to build a tool 
that would help my thief skills...

17:26.280 --> 17:28.050
But if you make it too thin, it snaps.

17:28.740 --> 17:31.680
And if you try to make it so it 
doesn't snap, it gets too thick!

17:31.680 --> 17:34.110
Making another weird item?

17:35.210 --> 17:37.560
I'm trying to come up with a way to deal 
with the traps in the new dungeon.

17:37.920 --> 17:41.530
I could do it faster with a picking tool,

17:41.530 --> 17:44.390
but it's hard to get one that's 
thin but doesn't break.

17:44.390 --> 17:46.440
Let me see that for a second.

17:51.780 --> 17:53.630
Well? How's this?

17:55.850 --> 17:57.290
Wow!

17:57.290 --> 17:58.670
I can tell you're a pro!

17:58.670 --> 18:01.260
It's even better than I could've hoped for!

18:01.530 --> 18:03.400
This one's on the house.

18:03.930 --> 18:07.000
Thanks! I learned a lot!

18:07.000 --> 18:09.070
Sure thing! Keep it up!

18:10.870 --> 18:13.440
<i>Things will go much smoother with this.</i>

18:13.440 --> 18:15.480
<i>Now I just need some more arrows...</i>

18:15.480 --> 18:18.210
Hey, how've you been?!

18:18.210 --> 18:20.220
You always show up out 
of nowhere, don't you?

18:20.220 --> 18:21.290
You scared me!

18:21.540 --> 18:25.320
Does that mean I should make a big 
announcement before I arrive?

18:25.320 --> 18:26.610
Maybe add in some music?

18:26.610 --> 18:28.450
Are you trying to be a pro wrestler?

18:28.750 --> 18:30.180
Well, whatever.

18:30.180 --> 18:33.380
So, you're in your full regalia today. 
Did something happen?

18:33.380 --> 18:37.400
I'm going to give out contract 
crystals to the new adventurers,

18:37.400 --> 18:39.920
so they can make contracts with fairies.

18:39.920 --> 18:43.550
Oh, right. A lot of new players just joined.

18:43.550 --> 18:46.940
I want to hand over as many as I can today.

18:46.940 --> 18:49.270
It's pretty tough to write all those emails.

18:49.270 --> 18:52.680
I do have human helpers, but still.

18:52.680 --> 18:57.230
<i>Does she mean the game's GMs?</i>

18:57.230 --> 19:01.790
<i>Still, going out of her way to deliver the 
crystals in person is pretty old-fashioned.</i>

19:02.020 --> 19:03.960
So, anyway, I'm off!

19:04.240 --> 19:07.910
Let's talk again later, my husband!

19:09.090 --> 19:11.920
You and I are <i>not</i> married!

19:11.920 --> 19:13.790
Aw, and I spent so much time on my hair.

19:14.620 --> 19:16.970
<i>She's a woman in that sense, I guess.</i>

19:16.970 --> 19:19.200
<i>Maybe I hit her too hard.</i>

19:19.200 --> 19:20.730
I guess it's time to go.

19:21.500 --> 19:23.690
Farewell!

19:25.870 --> 19:29.020
I guess she's working hard 
at her job, at least.

19:29.020 --> 19:31.280
I should work hard, too.

19:42.490 --> 19:45.940
This should be enough for 
another dungeon run.

19:45.940 --> 19:47.600
Now to do some cooking...

19:49.540 --> 19:51.490
I'm back...

19:52.560 --> 19:54.160
You don't look so good...

19:54.160 --> 19:57.720
Handing over the crystals went fine.

19:57.720 --> 19:59.680
But after that...

19:59.960 --> 20:02.740
Who cares about my measurements?

20:02.740 --> 20:05.000
Why do you want to know 
what kind of guy I like?

20:05.000 --> 20:06.830
What's the point of asking 
me my favorite food?

20:06.830 --> 20:09.570
And there were these weird questions 
about how I felt about having affairs,

20:09.570 --> 20:12.180
and I'm obviously not telling any of you 
where you can come meet me!

20:15.120 --> 20:18.150
I-I see. Sounds rough.

20:18.150 --> 20:22.020
I felt like I had no choice 
but to summon everyone

20:22.020 --> 20:24.370
who asked those questions 
to the battlefield,

20:24.370 --> 20:28.880
then defeat them and revive them ten times, 
giving them a death penalty each time.

20:28.880 --> 20:31.110
Wait... What were you thinking?

20:31.110 --> 20:33.000
But... But when I did...

20:33.000 --> 20:35.970
They said, "For us, this is a reward!"

20:35.970 --> 20:38.580
And then they all got these creepy smiles!

20:38.850 --> 20:41.050
Humans are scary.

20:41.050 --> 20:43.640
I'm so tired.

20:43.640 --> 20:46.480
<i>I do feel a little bad for her...</i>

20:46.480 --> 20:47.650
And so...

20:48.220 --> 20:49.970
Please, let me rest my head on your lap!

20:49.970 --> 20:51.420
Give me head pats!

20:51.420 --> 20:53.980
And sign this marriage form, too!

20:53.980 --> 20:56.520
Wh-Where did you learn about that?

20:56.520 --> 20:58.330
I got it from the town hall!

20:58.330 --> 21:00.380
I've already signed it!

21:00.380 --> 21:01.940
Which town hall?

21:01.940 --> 21:05.150
Once you sign it, 
we'll be officially married!

21:05.420 --> 21:06.980
Why would we get married?

21:06.980 --> 21:09.070
Sheesh, how do you learn about this stuff?

21:09.070 --> 21:11.050
Don't be so stubborn!

21:11.050 --> 21:14.010
The husband comes home tired from work!

21:14.010 --> 21:15.990
It's the wife's job to cheer the husband up!

21:15.990 --> 21:18.660
Who's the wife and who's the 
husband in this scenario?!

21:21.230 --> 21:23.060
It's so good!

21:23.060 --> 21:24.430
Sheesh...

21:24.430 --> 21:25.930
What's this called?

21:25.930 --> 21:27.890
I've never seen it before!

21:27.890 --> 21:29.040
It's a meat bun.

21:29.430 --> 21:31.930
My cooking skill finally hit level 50,

21:31.930 --> 21:33.560
and I can use a steamer now,

21:33.560 --> 21:34.720
so I tried making it.

21:35.090 --> 21:38.800
So I'm your first customer, huh?

21:38.800 --> 21:40.280
I'm so happy!

21:41.810 --> 21:46.180
<i>Well, I guess I can give her what 
she wants a little, just for today.</i>

21:46.180 --> 21:48.540
<i>It must be rough being a queen.</i>

21:48.540 --> 21:51.800
<i>She can't go on adventures 
whenever she wants like I can,</i>

21:51.800 --> 21:55.570
<i>and I'm the only adventurer 
she gets to talk to, so...</i>

21:55.570 --> 21:59.030
Thank you, husband!

21:59.790 --> 22:00.940
Stop saying that!

22:00.940 --> 22:02.770
Look at you blush!

22:03.560 --> 22:07.460
<i>Maybe I shouldn't have given 
her what she wanted... sob.</i>

22:07.470 --> 22:09.930
<b>To Be Continued</b>
